{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -l; nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '9,143p'\"","aggregated_output":"total 1008\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   16844 Nov 21 02:01 DESIGN.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    2823 Nov 21 01:59 census-dry.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     205 Nov 21 01:46 census-mutant.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    2223 Nov 21 01:46 claude-r13.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   12583 Nov 21 01:49 codex-r13.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  327300 Nov 21 01:49 codex-r13.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 21 02:01 codex-r14.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    7132 Nov 21 02:01 codex-r14.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    9229 Nov 21 01:51 expected-links.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   10529 Nov 21 01:51 expected-links.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    4481 Nov 21 01:51 expected_links.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   54399 Nov 21 01:41 neither-census.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    2758 Nov 21 01:41 neither.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    5685 Nov 21 02:00 read_census.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    3339 Nov 21 01:46 round13-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    2220 Nov 21 02:01 round14-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   12433 Nov 21 01:52 window_test.py\n     9\t4. does any other question get worse.\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. The shape: old-2 continued with links\n    12\t\n    13\tEvery request the linking version builds byte-equal to a request old-2 sent is answered with old-2's answer (each sequence works on its\n    14\town copy of old-2's archive); only the requests the links change are bought: the link questions (Jev) and the judgements of a question\n    15\tthat reads a linked question. This is the July test's method (`../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md`)\n    16\tover the whole window.\n    17\t\n    18\tWhy this shape and not an independent forward run:\n    19\t- **Question 4 is answered by construction and checked by code.** No other request carries a judgement of another question:\n    20\t  the extraction request shows open questions with their takes lines (`placement.question_lines`, `placement.takes`: key and group\n    21\t  only); Jev's matching state and thesis text show the question, its ladder and its first two pieces of evidence\n    22\t  (`jev_matching.candidate_state`, `thesis_text`, `matching.describe_view`); a judgement shows its own evidence, its own previous\n    23\t  conclusion, the theme block and its dependencies (`judging.build_prompt`). Linking writes only asset-to-asset rows (D695), so a\n    24\t  changed judgement reaches only the questions that read it. The July test confirmed it: three days, 39 bought calls, every other\n    25\t  request answered from the archive. The code check: every judgement of a question outside the reading chains is equal, row for row,\n    26\t  to old-2's.\n    27\t- **The links' effect is not buried in sampling noise.** A fresh run re-samples 1,884 extractions and about 1,600 judgements; the\n    28\t  questions opened and their evidence would differ from old-2's for reasons that have nothing to do with links.\n    29\t- **Cost:** only the readers' judgements and the link questions are bought (section 6), not the ~$9 of a fresh run.\n    30\t\n    31\tWhat this shape cannot show, stated with the result (round 13): it is a comparison **conditional on old-2's questions and evidence**;\n    32\thow the link step behaves on question sets another draw would open (only old-2's openings are asked); a fresh run's cost and timing;\n    33\tthe idea routes (they read judged positions and reasons, `idea.py`, and the daily replay does not call them: outside this measurement).\n    34\tThe equality check compares nine projections (`rebuild_control.compare`), and unrelated judgements are compared by question and day,\n    35\tsince extra reader judgements shift row ids. The archive matches a request by its canonical identity (sorted keys), as production's\n    36\tarchive does.\n    37\t\n    38\t## 2. The $0 proof that nothing else changes: the `neither` pass\n    39\t\n    40\t`window_test.py neither`: poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window, every link question answered \"neither\" by a fake Jev,\n    41\tevery other request from old-2's archive, anything else stops the pass. An answer old-2's own run refused (the archive keeps it under a\n    42\t`:refused:` suffix, four judge answers) is given back once, so the code refuses it again and the stored retry follows; without that,\n    43\tthe first pass stopped at 07-13 (v7, whose 07-13 judgement was a retry). The pass must end equal to old-2's finished store on views,\n    44\tkeys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements, switches, successions and dependencies (`rebuild_control.compare`), and it lists every\n    45\topening with the pairs shown and which are eligible under D695.\n    46\t\n    47\tResult (`neither.log`, `neither-census.json`; 375 seconds): **equal to old-2 in every table** (43 questions, 5,102 evidence items,\n    48\t6,306 evidence links, 1,616 judgements, 137 rungs, 44 switches, 2 successions, 0 dependencies; last completed seq 1884 in both); the\n    49\tfour refusals met again and none left unmet. The version asks link questions at **14 openings** (every new number question from v2 at\n    50\tseq 8 to v36 at seq 1262), **105 eligible pairs** in 14 jobs: each new number question against every earlier open number question of\n    51\tthe company (1, 2, ... 14 pairs; themes and yes/no questions are not eligible, D695). Openings with pairs:\n    52\t\n    53\t| seq | new question | pairs |\n    54\t|---|---|---|\n    55\t| 8 | v2 commitments for customer and cloud-provider guarantees, FY2027 | 1 |\n    56\t| 49 | v8 stand-alone CPU revenue FY2027 | 2 |\n    57\t| 62 | v9 Data Center revenue FY2027 | 3 |\n    58\t| 148 | v14 total revenue FY2027 | 4 |\n    59\t| 206 | v15 supply commitments, FY2027 report | 5 |\n    60\t| 265 | v16 total CPU revenue FY2027 | 6 |\n    61\t| 321 | v17 total revenue growth FY2028 | 7 |\n    62\t| 534 | v21 total revenue growth FY2027 | 8 |\n    63\t| 746 | v28 gross margin FY2027 | 9 |\n    64\t| 821 | v29 equity investment commitments, FY2027 report | 10 |\n    65\t| 1029 | v32 Poolside licence payment commitment | 11 |\n    66\t| 1102 | v33 gross margin FY2028 | 12 |\n    67\t| 1238 | v35 total revenue FY2028 | 13 |\n    68\t| 1262 | v36 MediaTek convertible-bond investment | 14 |\n    69\t\n    70\t## 3. Before any judgement is bought: the link decisions over the window\n    71\t\n    72\t**The July answers were close to a coin flip.** In each linked sequence Jev answered the 07-10 opening of v14 (total revenue FY2027)\n    73\tagainst v9 (Data Center FY2027): \"v9 reads v14\" 0.52, 0.54, 0.51; \"v14 reads v9\" 0.47, 0.45, 0.48. The rule takes Jev's choice at\n    74\t0.5 or more (`links.THRESHOLD`), so a shift of 0.02 gives no link or the opposite link. The same opening's v14–v8 (stand-alone CPU)\n    75\tpair: \"v14 reads v8\" 0.47, 0.46, 0.44 (below the line), \"neither\" ~0.40. JULY-RESULT.md reported the link \"chosen in 3 of 3\" without\n    76\tthese margins; this is added to it.\n    77\t\n    78\t**Mechanism (prompt audit, `links.READS_CRITERIA`):** \"candidate_reads_thesis\" covers \"a part read against its whole ... or a\n    79\tquantity read against another it depends on\"; for a total against its own segment, both readings fit: the segment is a part of the\n    80\ttotal, and the total depends on the segment. The documents carry both: D537 and council R name \"data-center revenue reading total\n    81\trevenue\" (a part reads its whole); PRD 06 (line 134, D368 by D208) says a historical seed's supported root reads its supporting\n    82\tdrivers. Verdict: **abstract** (one class, two directions with a source each).\n    83\t\n    84\t**The census** (`window_test.py census`, Jev only): the same whole-window pass with each link job sent to Jev as poc-v119 builds it\n    85\tand the writer handed no link, so no row is written and every later request stays old-2's (checked by the same equality). Three draws\n    86\tshare one reservation ledger, ceiling $0.10 (Jev reserved at its published 64K limit for each of its three attempts, as in July).\n    87\tIts $0 checks: `census-dry` (every eligible pair answered \"the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE\", sign together: 28 jobs, 105 links\n    88\tproposed, 0 written, equal to old-2 in every table, `census-dry.log`); the mutant (the same fake answers with links written) stops on\n    89\t07-01 at the first reader judgement, which misses the archive (`census-mutant.log`). Cost: 14 READS jobs of 1 to 14 questions per\n    90\tdraw plus the SIGN jobs of what passes; Jev input at $0.042 per million tokens.\n    91\tRead for every eligible pair: the answer and its probabilities in each draw; whether the chosen direction and sign are right under\n    92\tthe criterion's own examples; whether the decision is the same in 3 of 3 draws.\n    93\t\n    94\t**The registered reading (round 13: a gate needs a known positive, registered before any answer is read):** `expected_links.py` →\n    95\t`expected-links.md` / `.json` classes each of the 105 pairs: **R**, a required link with its direction, a part read against its whole\n    96\t(the READS criterion's own first example and D537): v1 reads v2, v9 reads v14, v8 reads v14, v16 reads v14, v8 reads v16 (5 pairs);\n    97\t**W**, any link wrong: a financing or commitment amount against a revenue, growth or margin question, or two financing amounts of\n    98\tdifferent kinds (57 pairs); **O**, defensible either way and reported only (43 pairs). The seq-148 pairs were seen before the\n    99\tregistration (the July answers), disclosed with every score. Round 13 corrected §3's sourcing: PRD 06 line 134 and D368 describe the\n   100\thistorical seed arrows and give no rule for a newly chosen number link; D537 is the source for the direction of a new one.\n   101\t\n   102\t**Scoring** (`read_census.py`, positive control on the fake answers: 58 wrong links found, gate FAIL): per pair and draw the READS and\n   103\tSIGN answers and the product's decision (a reading direction at 0.5 or more and a sign of together or opposite at 0.5 or more);\n   104\tR: right, missed or wrong (the opposite direction); W: wrong if linked; a margin below 0.10 on a linked or required pair is flagged\n   105\tfragile, not a gate. The three July answers count as three more draws of the seq-148 opening (the census rebuilds the same request,\n   106\tsha 6dcb7664…, `census-dry`).\n   107\t\n   108\t**Gate:** no wrong link in any draw, and v9 reads v14 linked in every draw. Pass: the paid design goes to its own council round on the\n   109\tcurrent wording, with the misses and the fragile pairs disclosed. Fail: the wrong-link class goes to the council; a wording that fixes\n   110\tthe part-and-whole direction changes what the system does and goes to Alex with options and a recommendation before any judgement is\n   111\tbought. Already known: v8 reads v14 was missed in all three July draws (the opposite direction at 0.47, 0.46, 0.44, below the line).\n   112\t\n   113\t**A draw counts only when complete** (`window_test.complete`): its READS answers are exactly the registered pairs, every READS answer\n   114\tthat passed has its SIGN answer, every job was answered, the pass ends equal to old-2 with no link row, and the ledger never stopped\n   115\tor overran. Mutants on the dry record: a dropped READS answer, a dropped SIGN answer and a failed job are each caught.\n   116\t\n   117\t**Budget:** each draw registers its launcher with the shared ledger (`claim_launcher`, so the stop gate stops every draw when one\n   118\tdies); the ledger is created with the ceiling Alex names and the harness refuses any other, a non-finite one, or one above $0.10\n   119\t(checked: NaN, 0 and 0.2 refused). The store is marked harness-only and held under its lock for the pass. Priced from the dry pass's\n   120\t28 jobs: the ledger settles a Jev call at three times its reported input (`budget_replay`), so a draw settles about $0.022 at most\n   121\t(tokens 0.37 of the request's bytes, the larger July ratio; every SIGN job included); three draws $0.066; the largest reservation\n   122\t$0.0084. The draws run one after another, so the live headroom is one reservation. Preflight: `dependency-design/preflight.log`\n   123\treplayed all of old-2's stored answers through the current checks (1,884 extraction rows, 61 matching records, the four stored judge\n   124\trefusals); the `neither` pass replays the whole window itself.\n   125\t\n   126\t## 4. The paid run (after the census, the council and Alex's ceiling)\n   127\t\n   128\t- **Linked, three sequences:** poc-v119, each on its own copy of old-2's archive and an empty ledger, the whole window. Jev's link\n   129\t  answers are not byte-stable (the July probabilities moved by up to 0.03), so the three may choose different links; each is read.\n   130\t- **Control, three sequences:** poc-v118 on its own archive copy with the judge rows of every reader of the linked sequences (their\n   131\t  union) retired from the seq of that reader's first link, so their judgements are fresh samples of the same requests old-2 sent.\n   132\t- **old-2's stored path** is a fourth control path, labelled: v9's self-made reference was found on it, so it is not a neutral draw.\n   133\t- Order: the three linked sequences first (they decide the readers), then the three controls. One shared reservation ledger under the\n   134\t  ceiling Alex names; a refused reservation or a stop makes the comparison inconclusive.\n   135\t- Each sequence uses the comparison runs' budget transport with July's settlement (cache writes at 1.25x), and an allow-list before\n   136\t  it: a sequence may buy only link questions and the judgements of its readers (linked) or of the retired readers (control); any other\n   137\t  request that misses the archive stops that sequence (July's latch).\n   138\t\n   139\tRound 13's points for the paid design's own round (not built yet): pair each control with its linked sequence and retire that\n   140\treader's original and retry requests from its first affected judgement, not the union; keep old-2 a labelled baseline outside the\n   141\tfresh-control mean; run the fresh calls together; report linked-only judgement days apart; record link choices that differ from the\n   142\tcensus.\n   143\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
